-- -----------------------------------------------------
-- NOTES: why the first block fails and how the fix works
-- The first block fails to compile because the label <<bonus_msg>>
-- is inside the IF ... END IF block, while the GOTO statement is
-- outside it. PL/SQL allows a GOTO to jump out of a block to a label
-- in an enclosing block, but it never allows a jump into an IF, LOOP,
-- CASE or nested block. Oracle reports this as PLS-00375.
-- In the fixed block I moved the label <<bonus_msg>> to the main
-- block and kept the GOTO inside the IF. The jump now leaves the IF,
-- which is legal, so the block compiles and prints the bonus message.
-- -----------------------------------------------------
